WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.490
I moved in yesterday.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.760
I didn't know you lived here.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.310
An incredible coincidence, isn't it?

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.580
A coincidence?

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.160
Or it could be fate.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:12.990
What?

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.920
The lower the chances of something are,

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.010
the more likely people are 
to feel it was fate. Right?

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.950
That may be true, but...

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.060
Sometimes, strange things 
happen in this world.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.810
To think the producer of the show 
<i>Miracle Finder</i> would be surprised by that.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.750
Wouldn't most people be surprised?

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.400
That aside, are you all right?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.290
You seem quite tired.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.160
I'm going to see the CEO of LFG today

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.130
to discuss the investigation
into financing our company,

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.060
but the report just wouldn't come together...

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.210
I'm sure it'll work out.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.610
And since I'm the one 
saying it, it's got to be true.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:47.780
I'll start thinking about how to celebrate.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.860
Thank you.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.960
But what do you mean by "celebrate"?

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.490
You'll just have to wait and see.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.220
<i>At this point, I was still...</i>

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:10.360
<i>My world was still just barely 
clinging to its peaceful slumber.</i>

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.510
<i>Now I know.</i>

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:16.970
<i>I know exactly how precious these 
innocent days were, and how fragile.</i>

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:28.270
"It takes all the running you can do, 
to keep in the same place."

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:28.270
~The Red Queen Hypothesis~

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.580
<i>In this world, there exist 
unique powers known as "Evol,"</i>

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.800
<i>which are possessed by a very few.</i>

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.280
<i>Among them, some chose to fight 
their fate, to fight the world.</i>

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.850
<i>This is the story of these young "Evolvers."</i>

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:03.950
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.390
"A Taste of Reminiscence"

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.720
Oh! I'm sorry.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.980
<i>Another strange dream...</i>

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.980
<i>Last time, what happened in the dream 
happened exactly the same way in real life...</i>

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.800
<i>And then...</i>

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.460
<i>Evolvers...</i>

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:56.250
<i>There might be people who 
have special powers, even here.</i>

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.960
<i>Maybe even someone like 
that boy from before.</i>

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:04.300
Finding the truth and
 showing it to everyone...

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.180
That's what my job is about.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:10.680
<i>No matter what it takes, I have to protect 
the company and continue the show!</i>

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:16.360
<b>Kiro 
</b>Good morning, Potato Chip Princess! 
I'm really looking forward to being on your show!

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.360
<i>Good morning, Potato Chip Princess!</i>

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.620
<i>I'm really looking forward 
to being on your show!</i>

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:21.580
<i>And I have to make sure 
to keep this promise, too.</i>

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.320
<i>Okay! I can do this!</i>

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:25.450
<b>Miracle Finder!
 </b>Program Plan

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.450
Are you an idiot?

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.410
<i>Miracle Finder</i> is a program with
 an originality found nowhere else.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.050
However, due to its niche content,

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:36.620
the current major TV stations will not 
approve the production of such a show.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.190
Therefore, first,

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:41.300
a web series within your 
company's production capabilities

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.760
will be used to expand the fanbase.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.940
I understand up to this point.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.530
But what I want to know 
is what happens after that.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.680
If you hope to emphasize the 
strength of your segments

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.970
to avoid being buried by the 
mountain of potential content,

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.390
then prepare a concrete proposal 
that will show me this.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.310
I'm sorry.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.890
To stand at the top of the 
industry in five years...

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:00.900
To make me eat my own words...

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.440
No matter how stupid you might be, 
I'm sure you remember.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.450
<i>Oh, come on! Does he really 
have to call me stupid?</i>

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.570
If you have a rebuttal, then speak.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:10.610
I do not.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.780
I was unable to prepare 
properly for today,

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:16.050
but next time, I will have
 something that you'll approve.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:17.960
Will you?

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:21.210
Idiots tend to make statements like 
that without thinking them through.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.990
<i>I know I'm in the wrong here.</i>

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:28.180
<i>But this nagging jerk makes me so angry!</i>

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.220
<i>I won't let him beat me, though!</i>

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.600
<i>I will continue the show and find the 
truth about Black Swan, no matter what!</i>

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.310
<i>Wait a minute...</i>

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:39.520
Did you discuss what happened
 this afternoon with anyone?

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.300
<i>What if the CEO is connected to Black Swan?</i>

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.900
<i>What if he's deliberately trying to hinder me?</i>

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.910
Did some good idea suddenly occur to you?

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:54.460
Sir, you... wouldn't be trying to 
prevent me from making my show

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:57.790
by pretending to be an arrogant, 
obnoxious person, would you?

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.120
Are you listening? 
I won't say it a third time.

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:07.670
No idiot would invest in 
something with no future.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:11.720
If you intend to create an idiotic
 show for idiots made by idiots,

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:12.810
then look elsewhere.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.460
I seriously can't believe this!

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.660
Why would you go out of your way 
to make his impression of us worse?

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:24.710
Please stop. I get it already.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:27.180
For now, let's gather up the 
program plans we have here.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.490
Any that might give us a hint.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.130
Will do.

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:32.160
We do have one trump card to play.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.150
If we can come up with an 
interesting idea for an episode,

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.660
Kiro will appear on the program.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.040
What?!

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:44.500
"Whether You Have the Best of Memories
or the Worst of Traumas,

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.930
Let's Go to Souvenir Restaurant."

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.170
Is this yours, Kiki-chan?

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.000
Yes!

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.510
The reviews for that restaurant 
are really interesting!

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.850
Every reviewer rates the food really highly,

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.030
but the restaurant itself 
is rated really low.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:00.370
Overall Impression <b>1.24
</b>Food・Flavor <b>4.95</b>

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:05.000
sue88(1279)'s review 

00:06:57.030 --> 00:07:00.230
<i>"The pudding is alive! If I'm not careful, 
it might run right out of my mouth!"</i>

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:05.820
chanshiii(85)'s review 
Overall Impression <b>1.5
</b>Food・Flavor <b>5.0 

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.770
<i>"This place is the absolute worst! 
But I just keep going back!"</i>

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:05.820
purin0820man(13)'s review 
Overall Impression <b>1.1
</b>Food・Flavor <b>4.9 
Just shut up and sell the pudding!</b>

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:05.840
<i>"Just shut up and sell the pudding!"</i>

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:07.140
Pudding...

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:09.240
That seems to be their hottest item.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.450
The miraculous idol who charms us all, Kiro,

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.240
and the miraculous food 
created by a much-hated chef...

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:19.070
If we can combine these two ideas 
and what led us to them,

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:20.880
and present them together...

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.880
That sounds great! I want to see that!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.340
I'll write a proposal by tomorrow morning!

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.310
It's so hot...

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:35.450
<i>I heard!</i>

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.680
<i>They said you're bringing 
over a proposal tomorrow!</i>

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.430
"I was thinking of buying 
something to bring,

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:40.430
I was thinking of buying 
something to bring,

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.900
but it can't be anything sweet, right?"

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:48.030
<b>Kiro
 </b>I think my manager would get mad...

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.030
"I think my manager would get mad..."

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:52.540
"But if it were homemade or something, 
he might just overlook it..."

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.950
"Just kidding!"

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:59.360
I could make pudding...

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:04.580
It's so hot, the pudding's going to melt.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.540
I'd better hurry and get it to them.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:13.820
Gavin-senpai!

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.340
You working?

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.930
Yes. I'm headed over to Loveland TV.

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.450
What about you?

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:21.560
Just coming off night shift. 
I'll take you there.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.500
What? You really—

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:30.740
Um, I appreciate the thought, but...

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:34.770
If an Evolver shows up, 
you have to let me know.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:36.020
I will.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:38.910
As it happens, I see one right in front of me.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.150
It's true that I'm an Evolver,

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.830
but I would never hurt you.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.610
O-Okay...

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.680
I barely made it in ti—

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:11.190
Why are you here?

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:13.810
Meeting with the board of directors.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:15.900
We have investments here, too.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.710
I see.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:21.360
It fell apart!

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.080
And I went to the trouble of making it!

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:24.860
You made that?

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:26.380
Yes, I did.

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:29.380
So you were focused on making pudding 
instead of drafting your plan.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.260
<i>Seriously! Does he have 
to say things that way?</i>

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.340
<i>No, no, no, no. Don't get angry. Don't get angry.</i>

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:41.680
This was meant to help facilitate 
the negotiations for our next episode.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.430
But now it's ruined.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.240
Are you trying to say it was my fault?

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.790
Certainly not! Who would say 
such a thing to the CEO?

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:51.940
There is a particular temperature 
at which pudding should be eaten.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:53.450
Its appearance aside,

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:56.150
ask that it is at least 
chilled before it is eaten.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:56.990
Huh?

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:58.950
Hey!

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:00.870
Kiro!

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:02.620
An Evolver...

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:04.400
Kiro is...

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:06.890
Good work today.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:07.720
You, too.

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:10.000
Though I'm not sure if he's 
even aware of it himself.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:12.460
I'll be waiting for your report.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.620
Uh, yes, sir.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.480
You came, Potato Chip Princess!

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:17.470
What's wrong?

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:19.720
Nothing!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.930
Thank you for today. I brought this!

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:24.640
Woohoo! It's what you 
were talking about, right?

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.360
It got a little broken up, though.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:29.410
If you can, chill it before you eat it.

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:30.640
Thanks!

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:33.420
I'll leave it to chill in the green 
room fridge until I'm done filming.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.610
<b>Mr. Kiro</b>

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.610
"Souvenir," is it?

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.440
You've heard of it?

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:41.070
Well, I <i>am</i> a regular there!

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:41.870
What?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:45.520
But speaking as someone 
who knows the place well...

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:48.430
Honestly, I think this 
project will be difficult.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:52.470
Interviews and news coverage 
are completely off-limits there.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:54.670
And it's impossible to know 
when it will be open.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:57.880
I'll go every day, starting today, 
and I'll get their permission.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.540
It isn't a question of perseverance.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.590
Many production companies have tried—

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.830
There is no tomorrow for us!

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.330
We're betting the fate of 
our company on this project!

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:11.760
I see.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.480
Then if you can obtain Souvenir's permission,

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.850
I promise Kiro will appear on your show.

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:18.550
Thank you so much!

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.450
Found it.

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:32.170
I suppose it wouldn't be that easy.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:34.420
I'll come back tomorrow!

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:46.910
Done!

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.180
I can finally eat this!

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.800
Just this once, okay?

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:52.140
Thanks!

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.600
I'll up my training to make up for it.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:58.150
Hey, it's not broken up at all!

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.030
It's so yummy!

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:16.100
It's disgusting.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.970
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:28.970
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.270
You can't be serious. Today's the fourth day!

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:39.820
<i>What will I do? The board 
review meeting is tomorrow!</i>

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.160
Welcome.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:46.500
You are a customer, I presume?

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.370
Oh, um, yes!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.860
Are you the owner of this restaurant?

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:55.670
I serve as a waiter here. My name is Mills.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:00.420
Please, come inside.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:01.800
Thank you!

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.230
<i>Finally, I can go inside!</i>

00:13:05.230 --> 00:13:07.300
<i>I promise I'll get permission 
to do a story on them!</i>

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.430
Excuse me, is the kitchen...

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:22.810
The owner is there.

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:25.500
He also serves as the chef 
of this establishment.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:26.960
I see.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:28.490
U-Um...

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:31.050
The truth is, I'm from this company.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:34.090
Would you let us do a story on your restaurant?

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:38.440
The owner doesn't like 
this sort of thing, I'm afraid.

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:41.980
I know requests to cover this 
restaurant are usually refused.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:45.880
But is there any way he might 
at least listen to what I have to say?

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:50.000
If you'll wait just a moment.

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:03.150
My apologies. I must ask you to leave for today.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.110
What?

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:07.920
The owner has said he will 
not accept you as a customer.

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.570
Wait... Just a moment!

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:11.990
If you would please take your leave.

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:13.630
This can't be...

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:16.470
I ran all the way here!

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.010
I'm exhausted...

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:19.420
Hello, Grandpa Mills.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.950
Welcome.

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:21.880
How...

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.940
I'm off today!

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:26.010
When I heard this place 
was open, I came flying!

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.010
Have you ordered yet?

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:30.840
I, um...

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.770
Did you start talking about doing a story 
as soon as you got here and get kicked out?

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:39.970
I've seen that happen to lots of people.

00:14:42.050 --> 00:14:43.700
This is a restaurant.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:45.400
It's a place to have a meal.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:50.160
I've only been thinking of myself...

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.420
It was rude to ask before I'd even eaten.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.320
It's no wonder the owner was angry.

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:58.160
I'm truly sorry.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:01.830
Grandpa Mills, couldn't you 
at least let her eat? For my sake?

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:02.750
Please?

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.620
I suppose it can't be helped.

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:09.760
I'll take the brunt of
 the owner's ire this time.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.320
Yes! Thank you!

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.010
Thank you very much!

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:18.680
If the owner here dislikes 
you even a little bit,

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.960
he'll throw you out, even if you're still eating.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:24.110
So that's why their reputation is so bad.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:27.330
But the food is unbelievably 
delicate and nuanced!

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:32.550
The owner sends out the dishes 
at the precise temperature

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.070
that makes them the most delicious.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:39.270
Please, enjoy your meal.

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:42.450
Thank you for this meal.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:49.970
What is this? It's unbelievable!

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:00.880
Hey, did you learn how to make 
that pudding from someone?

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:03.400
No. I'm completely self-taught.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.650
Then you're really gonna be surprised!

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:06.400
Try a taste!

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:15.390
What do you think?

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:17.090
It's exactly the same as yours, right?

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:21.290
Is something wrong?

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:26.170
Potato Chip Princess?

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.960
Oh... I-I'm sorry.

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:31.670
Are you okay?

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:34.070
Yeah. I'm really sorry.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:35.200
I'm fine.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:38.390
I've never seen someone cry 
because their food was so good.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:45.350
This flavor... It's the taste of the most 
delicious pudding I've had in my life.

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:52.240
The thing is... I don't have any memories 
from before the age of five.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.070
What do you mean?

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:58.410
I was involved in a kidnapping...

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:02.540
And it seems I received some kind 
of severe shock at that time.

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:07.060
There's just one thing I do remember, though.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:13.190
The taste of some delicious pudding 
I ate somewhere before I turned five.

00:17:13.190 --> 00:17:17.230
I started making pudding because 
I wanted to hold on to that memory,

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.430
but I never managed to find it.

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:22.530
Yours was just as delicious, though!

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:23.880
Not at all.

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:26.770
I've never made anything 
that tasted this good.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:35.220
Did our food suit your tastes?

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:37.570
It was incredibly moving! Truly!

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:42.910
Mr. Mills...

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:46.750
Would you allow me to do 
a story on this restaurant?

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.080
Please!

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:52.060
Miss, I believe I told you—

00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:54.220
I promise I'll make it a good show!

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:58.950
Making food that can 
move people this deeply

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.220
is certainly no easy feat.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:06.260
Through my show, I want to 
convey that feeling to everyone.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:10.810
Won't you please help me take
the first step on that path?

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.980
Please! I beg you!

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:28.870
<b>Kiro 
</b>I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.870
<i>I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.</i>

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:31.640
Not at all. Thank you for so much.

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:35.950
<i>I have to hurry back to the office 
and think about my next move.</i>

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:44.720
<b>Regarding your request for an interview

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.190
Huh?

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.740
Why are you here?

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:08.330
Could it be that you're a regular here, too?

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:09.810
I mean...

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:11.620
Really? It's <i>you</i>?!

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:17.820
Just so you're aware,

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.840
it isn't me you'll be interviewing. 
It will be Mr. Mills.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.380
Understood.

00:19:22.380 --> 00:19:24.840
But why are you...

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:27.180
I've always liked cooking.

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:31.200
Alone, I focus all five senses 
to find the most logical path.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:34.450
Working to achieve an ideal 
is a pleasant feeling for me.

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:35.980
A sort of change of pace?

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.480
Is that all?

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:41.240
I'm looking for someone.

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:44.120
There was a possibility
 that this may lead to a clue.

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:47.300
Making food might lead to a clue?

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.160
Um...

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:53.420
It was the very faintest of possibilities.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.120
I see.

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:59.030
The food was made with that person in mind.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.260
Um, may I ask one question?

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:08.310
Have you never thought of 
using your Evolver powers

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:11.000
to give you an advantage?

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.980
Why would I go to that much trouble?

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:16.370
I will use my own quick wit 
to break through any walls

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:17.900
and go as far as I can go.

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:21.280
I will go as far as I can go, too.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:23.840
The deadline is tomorrow.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:26.060
Don't waste my time.

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:26.870
I won't.

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:34.400
Congratulations on the 
funding being resumed!

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.270
Yay!

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:36.520
Well done!

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:38.090
She really did great.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:43.340
<b>Kiro 
</b>Congrats! I'm already super looking 
forward to making an appearance. 
Let's make it a good show!

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:39.630
<i>Congrats!</i>

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:42.050
<i>I'm already super looking 
forward to making an appearance.</i>

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.340
<i>Let's make it a good show!</i>

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.850
All right, all right! Listen up, everyone!

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:49.570
Our president has something to say.

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:50.370
What?

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:56.510
Thank you for everything, everyone! Truly!

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:59.690
We're finally standing at the starting line.

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:04.950
We've overcome this crisis and 
become stronger than before.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:08.030
I have every confidence we 
can make a meaningful show.

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:10.680
The real fight starts now!

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:12.200
Let's give it everything we've got!

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:13.840
Yeah!

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:19.030
I didn't know there was a place like this!

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:20.460
Do you like it?

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:21.480
Yes!

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:25.200
But I never thought you'd 
actually celebrate with me.

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:29.300
I said right at the start that 
I knew it would work out, didn't I?

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:37.980
This is my congratulations to you.

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:41.050
I heard there was a fireworks show today.

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:43.150
It's a little far away, though.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:45.640
It's like we have box seats!

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:10.720
Thank you for today. I know you 
must be busy with your research.

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:12.790
This is part of my research.

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:15.970
I'm very interested in you, you see.

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:16.940
Huh?

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:19.760
If I had to explain it, I'd say as a lab animal.

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:20.930
What?

00:22:20.930 --> 00:22:22.230
I'm kidding.

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:25.490
However, it is true 
that I'm interested in you.

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:28.100
I wonder what path you'll take from here.

00:22:29.470 --> 00:22:32.660
I want to keep making good shows,

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:35.480
and one day, find the truth behind Evolvers.

00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:37.940
I'll help you.

00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:39.040
Thank you.

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:52.070
Senpai?

00:22:55.530 --> 00:22:56.350
It can't be!

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:02.760
He's dangerous. Stay behind me.

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:05.510
What?

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:07.780
Lucien?

00:23:21.330 --> 00:23:25.060
<i>The key to the experiment lay in 
a place I never could have imagined.</i>

00:23:25.060 --> 00:23:28.810
<i>It's precisely because we're in the dark 
that certain things are possible.</i>

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:30.740
<i>Episode four,</i>

00:23:30.740 --> 00:23:32.480
<i>"The Key in the Darkness."</i>

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:34.970
"The Key in the Darkness"
